iv></div></h1><p><span>On December 2, 2025, one day after the DeepSeek V3.2=
 release, the Mistral team released their new </span><a href=3D"https://mis=
tral.ai/news/mistral-3">Mistral 3</a><span> model suite. This includes thre=
e smaller dense models (3B, 8B, and 14B) under the Ministral 3 name, as wel=
l as their new Mistral 3 Large flagship model, which is a 675B parameter Mo=
E (with 41B parameters active). More specifically, the Mistral 3 Large mode=
l consists of</span></p><ul><li><p>An MoE Language Model with 673B params a=
nd 39B active</p></li><li><p>A 2.5B Vision Encoder</p></li></ul><p><span>(S=
ince this article focuses on the LLM aspects, we will ignore the vision enc=
oder in this section. I should perhaps update my </span><a href=3D"https://=
magazine.sebastianraschka.com/p/understanding-multimodal-llms">multimodal L=
LMs article</a><span> sometime, though.)</span></p><p>First, it=E2=80=99s i=
nteresting to note that it=E2=80=99s Mistral=E2=80=99s first MoE since Mixt=
ral in 2023 (earlier in this article, I wrote that Mistral abandoned MoEs, =
and DeepSeek V3 last year ushered in an MoE revival). </p><p>The release bl=
og article says that all model sizes come in base, instruct, and reasoning =
variants, which is nice. However, their reasoning version of their 675B mod=
el is not available yet. </p><p><span>Another interesting tidbit is that Mi=
stral partnered with NVIDIA here to optimize tokens/sec throughput on Black=
well chips, </span><a href=3D"https://mistral.ai/news/mistral-3">according =
to their announcement</a><span>. This is nice because it means the Ministra=
l models will run a bit faster than comparable models on my little DGX Spar=
k (I still have to test this).</span></p><p>Besides the token/sec speed adv=
antage of Mistral 3, based on quality benchmarks, though their smaller mode=
ls, Ministral, look on par with Qwen3. The larger flagship model is on par =
with DeepSeek V3.1.</p><p>Since the release of Mistral 3 was just one day a=
fter DeepSeek V3.2=E2=80=99s release, they didn=E2=80=99t include any V3.2 =
comparisons in their article (except for the LMArena Elo score, where DeepS=
eek V3.2 is slightly ahead with 1423 vs 1418).</p><p><span>Unfortunately, i=
t=E2=80=99s not possible to do an apples-to-apples comparison right now, be=
cause Mistral 3 Large currently doesn=E2=80=99t have a reasoning model, and=
 DeepSeek V3.2 didn=E2=80=99t share the benchmark results for their non-thi=
nking mode, but in case you are curious, I overlaid the DeepSeek V3.2-Think=
ing numbers (from the </span><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.02556">D=
eepSeek V3.2 report</a><span>) with the Mistral 3 Large benchmark chart.</s=
pan></p><div class=3D"captioned-image-container"><figure><a target=3D"_blan=
